// edit the recipe, not this file.
page RecipeActiveTabInTheAddress(path: "/recipes/active-tab-in-the-address", title: "Keep the active tab in the address — Recipes", description: "Keep the active tab in the address's #fragment, so it survives a reload and a shared link opens on the same tab.") {
    RecipeShell("Keep the active tab in the address", summary: "A tab held in a `state` goes back to the first one on every reload. To make the tab survive a reload, and a shared link open on the same tab, read it from the address's `#fragment`:", outputs: ["website", "app"], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works")], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Build a confirm dialog", to: "/recipes/confirm-dialog"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Copy to the clipboard", to: "/recipes/copy-to-the-clipboard"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Count down", to: "/recipes/count-down")], source: "md-docs/recipes/active-tab-in-the-address.md", how: true, hasVariations: false) {
        code {
            CodeBlock(#"page Account(path: "/account", title: "Account", description: "Your profile and billing.") {
    derived tab = if hash != "" { hash } else { "profile" }
    Heading("Account").h1
    Row(gap: .sm) {
        Link("Profile", to: "/account#profile")
        Link("Billing", to: "/account#billing")
    }
    if tab == "profile" { Text("Profile settings") }
    if tab == "billing" { Text("Billing settings") }
}"#, title: "wf")
        }
        Markdown("- [`hash`](/learn/05-pages-and-routing#query-strings-and-fragments) is the address's fragment without the `#`, kept current by the runtime.\n- `tab` is a [`derived`](/learn/07-state-and-reactivity#derived) value: the fragment when there is one, `\"profile\"` when there is none.\n- Each tab is a `Link` to the same page with another fragment. Following it changes `hash`, `tab` follows, and the matching `if` draws its panel. The back button steps through the tabs the reader opened.\n\nTo keep several settings in the address, such as a sort and a filter, use the query string instead: see [Keep filters in the address](/recipes/filters-in-the-address).")

    }
}
